{"title":"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video(By_YippieMath)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video(By YippieMath)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangular garden 60 feet long and 20 feet wide is enclosed by a fence. To make the garden larger, while using the same fence, its shape is changed to a square. By how many square feet does this enlarge the garden?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1e21795a63b2fb996f16e401ade587e656f848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 100 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 200 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 300 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 400 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"421\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We need the same perimeter as a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> rectangle, but the greatest area we can get. right now the perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b921eebe6fcb6019117772839fa2aa142827e703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$160$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. To get the greatest area while keeping a perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b921eebe6fcb6019117772839fa2aa142827e703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$160$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, the sides should all be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. that means an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc314f9ecb9c2b3c96a327f5191f1d5b13d8e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1600$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. Right now, the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6eeed1fb9399450cfcd051673ecb35215809ddf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\times 60$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e0588c55c2d51f1677c8bd4a06da1d49197ce4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1200$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc72fa5271089d90ac2b8163c431ee85480aac35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1600-1200=400$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"145\" height=\"13\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We need the same perimeter as a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> rectangle, but in a square. Right now the perimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b921eebe6fcb6019117772839fa2aa142827e703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$160$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, since a square has equal sides and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b921eebe6fcb6019117772839fa2aa142827e703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$160$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> divided by 4 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />,  the sides should all be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, that means an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/c/6cc314f9ecb9c2b3c96a327f5191f1d5b13d8e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1600$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. Before, the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6eeed1fb9399450cfcd051673ecb35215809ddf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 \\times 60$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e0588c55c2d51f1677c8bd4a06da1d49197ce4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1200$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc72fa5271089d90ac2b8163c431ee85480aac35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1600-1200=400$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"145\" height=\"13\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video.28By_YippieMath.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video(By_YippieMath)\">Video(By YippieMath)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video(By YippieMath)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=glxI3hrkAlA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=glxI3hrkAlA</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8\" title=\"1999 AMC 8\">1999 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016233141\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 179/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2268/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3898/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.023      1 -total\n 57.75%    6.943      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 40.51%    4.871      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9589:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016233141 an